SUMMARY:National Day of Remembrance and Action on Violence Against Women
DESCRIPTION:December 6 is the National Day of Remembrance and Action on Violence Against Women. \nMark the day on Monday\, December 7 with memorial events and activities across campus.\nAll are welcome to join. \n  \nDrop-in Memorial & Self-Guided Tour | Dec 7\, 11 am – 12 pm\nHosted by U of T’s Sexual Violence Prevention & Support Centre\, join a moment of reflection at the Ziibiing Pavilion at 11 am. Firekeepers will be present to tend a ceremonial fire\, and white roses will be available to honour those lost to gener-based violence. Following this brief memorial\, all participants are welcome to join a self-guided walk around campus to other points of interest. Learn more on the SVPS Centre website. \nStudent-led ceremony at U of T Engineering | Dec 7\, 6 – 7 pm\nJoin the U of T Engineering community on the steps of the Galbraith Building at 6pm for a student-led ceremony to honour the lives of the 14 women killed at Montreal’s École Polytechnique in 1989. To mark the 37th anniversary of this devastating act of misogyny\, we will join together in collective grief for all those lost to gender-based violence as we remember those who were killed\, and look toward a better future. \nWant to get involved? Build days and ceremony planning take place on November 21\, 22\, 28\, 29 and Dec 5 in the Myhal Centre’s EngSoc Arena. Drop in any time to help build this year’s display (no experience required).\n \n 
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/national-day-of-remembrance-and-action-on-violence-against-women-7/
LOCATION:Galbraith Building\, 35 St George St\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 1A4\, Canada
END:VEVENT
